  "term": "treatment level",
  "definition": "Treatment level means an amount or concentration used in therapeutic use, such as the doses commonly used in preclinical or clinical studies, rather than unusually high amounts. In this source, it refers to concentrations intended for treatment and contrasts with extreme concentrations that produced different effects.",
